**Why will this work in Unity?**

This approach explicitly captures the type information of each element in a list, allowing you to reconstruct the exact list with the correct element types during deserialization. It avoids the compiler's requirement for a known generic type argument by storing the type alongside the value. This makes your serialization compatible with any list type (since you store the `Type` of each element), and arrays are handled by storing their values directly.

